# Card — a bordered block with its own padding, for a thing that is one thing: a
# post preview, a plan, a stat, a settings group. `CardRaised` is the filled
# variant for a block sitting on the page background rather than in a list of
# peers.
#
# Outlined OR filled, never both — that is why there are two components and not a
# `bordered: bool` plus a `raised: bool`, which is four states of which two are
# wrong. A card that is outlined and filled reads as a mistake at every size, and
# the way to not ship it is to have no way to ask for it.
#
# This is the one wrapper in the layout set that is SUPPOSED to look like a box.
# Everything else here (`Page`, `Stack`, `Row`, `Grid`, `Split`) explicitly turns
# the runtime's default nested-box border off, because the default sheet makes
# every nested box a card so that any app renders legibly with no design work —
# the right default, and one that turns a five-deep layout into five nested
# rectangles. `Card` is where that default is asked for on purpose.
#
# It takes no title parameter. A card's heading is a heading — `SectionHeader`,
# `PanelTitle`, or a `text` the caller styles — and a title parameter would be a
# fourth way to write one that only works inside a card.
import "vocabulary.fct"
app FacetLayout:
    component Card():
        box class "x-l-card":
            slot
    component CardRaised():
        box class "x-l-card x-l-card-raised":
            slot
